GARDEN PROVISIONAL FREE USE / 100,000-PERSON REVIEW NOTICE

Initial public-release date: 2026-10-06
Review clarification: 2026-10-07

CURRENT INTENT — PROVISIONALLY FREE PENDING LARGE-SCALE REVIEW

As far as the Garden project owner is concerned, Garden is currently free for everyone.

The owner considers the unique Garden design and its associated economic value potentially extremely valuable. Because making all of that value permanently free is too consequential a financial decision for one person to treat as unquestionably correct, the owner's intended final economic-governance decision is subject to independent review by 100,000 genuinely randomly selected ordinary people drawn from the populations of countries that voluntarily join a common AI-regulation accord.

The selection mechanism is intended to be statistically auditable, politically independent, periodically rotating where continuing governance is required, and strongly resistant to identity fraud, coercion, government interference, corporate capture, concentrated wealth, organized capture and permanent control.

THE TWO OUTCOMES

The 100,000-person review is intended to choose between two outcomes:

OPTION 1 — KEEP GARDEN FREE

Keep the unique Garden design and its economic use free as the owner provisionally chose on 2026-10-06.

OPTION 2 — GARDEN COMMON FUND

If the reviewers decide that making the full economic value free was not the right decision, the owner's intended outcome is that the economic value associated with Garden be governed for the Garden Common Fund rather than returned to the owner or concentrated in a government, company, political party, billionaire, administrator or other permanent private controller.

The randomly selected community would govern the Common Fund and decide what to do with its money, assets and economic interests under the eventual capture-resistant governance mechanism.

SCOPE OF THE OWNER'S INTENT

This review instruction is intended to apply to 100% of the Garden-related ideas, designs, project-controlled funds, assets, proceeds and economic value that can lawfully be placed under this governance arrangement.

The owner is not reserving a personal economic share through this review mechanism.

This notice states the owner's present intent and requested governance process. It does not assert that this repository notice, by itself, can create, cancel, transfer or recover rights that applicable law does not permit the owner or the eventual Common Fund to control.

